# The user's repos and how to work on them

## Where the code lives
- **GitLab is the source of truth:** `git@gitlab.com:{{ agent_git_owner }}/<repo>.git`. Use only this as a remote.
- **GitHub (`{{ agent_git_owner }}/<repo>`) is a read-only copy.** GitLab pushes `main` there after the user merges,
  and deploys build from GitHub. Never add GitHub as a remote or push there.
- **Your access:** the SSH key `~/.ssh/{{ agent_git_key_name }}` is a GitLab deploy key. It can clone and push branches.
  It has no API: no `glab`, no issues, no MR comments, no merging. `main` is protected; a rejected push to it is expected.

